 ### <a id="orcl-sec-005"></a>ORCL-SEC-005: JPY/USD shared dependency failsafe
 
 - Type: Security
-- Statement: The JPY/USD oracle is shared by every branch and has the widest blast radius. A JPY-leg failure must therefore not cause immediate terminal shutdown. Exactly one `JpyUsdRateProvider` is deployed and injected into every active source; inherited or duplicated per-feed state is prohibited because it cannot provide shared storage. The provider stores `lastGoodJpyRate` with the same response's `lastGoodJpyUpdatedAt`, and on first failure sets `jpyFrozenSince = min(block.timestamp, lastGoodJpyUpdatedAt + PRM-ORACLE-001)`. Every branch therefore receives the same frozen rate, onset, recovery, and expiry decision. Recovery inside `PRM-ORACLE-006` resumes live rates automatically. Expiry is latched before returning it to consumers, so later Chainlink recovery cannot treat only branches that have not yet observed the failure as recovered; each active branch transitions through its standard `lastGoodPrice` shutdown path on its next fetch. When a source is behind `PriceFeedProxy`, it catches the expected source-level BorrowerOperations caller-mismatch on this path and returns `failure=true`; the registered Proxy performs shutdown in the same transaction. This preserves the provider latch instead of reverting all state changes. Collateral, peg-monitor, canonical-rate, and backing failures remain branch-local terminal failures and are evaluated before JPY fallback. Monitor the provider address/state/events (`JpyRateFrozen`, `JpyRateUnfrozen`, `JpyFreezeExpired`) externally and fail deployment/preflight if active sources reference different providers.
-- Verification: unit (cached-rate timestamp provenance, immediate shutdown for stale and invalid responses on the first call after the freeze limit elapses with no traffic, first-observation anchoring while the cached rate is fresh, recovery within 24h, standard and sUSDS implementations), integration (Proxy path), fork (JPY/USD staleness), manual (heartbeat × N and weekend update history finalization)
